{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
It's been [A]ten long [C#7]years since [D]I left my [A]home
In the [A]holler where I was [E]born
Where the [A]cool fall [C#7]nights make the [D]wood smoke [A]rise
And the [A]fox hunter [E]blows his [A]horn
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I fell in love with a girl from the town
I thought that she would be true
I ran away to Charlottesville
And worked in a sawmill or two
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[E]What have they done to the [A]old home place?
[B]Why did they tear it [E]down?
And why [A]did I leave [C#7]my plow [D]in the [A]field?
[A]And look for [E]a job in [A]the town?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Well, the girl ran off with somebody else
The tariffs took all my pay
And here I stand where the old home stood
Before they took it away
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
Now the geese fly south and the cold wind blows
As I stand here and hang my head
I've lost my love, I've lost my home
And now I wish that I was dead
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
Chorus        (tag out or solos and repeat chorus)
{end_of_verse}
